nt aggregation; geopolitical disruptions affecting tourism; slow rollout of Amrit Bharat pre-paid catering","src":"concall","title":"Risks & watch-items"},{"body":"Confident and forward-looking; emphasized digital transformation, volume-led growth, and strategic moats (payment aggregator, unified portal); transparent on challenges (debtor days, station upgrades); optimistic on MICE and tourism scalability","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"IRCTC’s internal payment volume (Rs. 13,000cr GMP) is only 20% of its potential (Rs. 70,000cr), indicating massive untapped monetization opportunity once RBI license is granted; MICE events are being structured as cluster-based PPPs with govt ministries — not just tourism, but a new B2G revenue stream","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"}],"business":[{"body":"Internet Ticketing: Rs. 386cr (+4% YoY), 89.24% market share, EBITDA margin 85%; Catering: Rs. 520cr (+8% YoY), margin 13%; Rail Neer: Rs. 91cr (+4.6% YoY), margin 10%; Tourism: Rs. 150cr (+20.97% YoY), margin improved to 7% (from negative YoY); MICE: New vertical, 8% minimum margin target","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| IRCTC’s payment aggregator license approval | IRCTC | beneficiary | High | Could unlock Rs. 500-700cr+ annual revenue from payment processing fees on 13.5cr+ monthly transactions, transforming IRCTC from rail service provider to fintech platform |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"EBITDA margin improved to 35.25% due to digital ticketing efficiency (85% margin) and tourism cost rationalization; catering margins stable at 13% despite input cost pressures; volume-driven pricing strategy (e.g., Rs. 14 Rail Neer, Rs. 80 meals) avoids price hikes","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"Revenue growth: Sustained mid-single digit; margin: Stable to expand via cost efficiency; order inflow: MICE and Bharat Gaurav trains; capex/commissioning: Bilaspur plant (72K bottles/day) to restart; Danapur/Ambernath upgraded to 3L bottles/day; 4 new plants planned","src":"concall","title":"Guidance"},{"body":"Not disclosed","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"Payment aggregator business (RBI in-principle approval secured); unified travel portal with AI/ML; cross-selling via IRCTC’s 13.55cr quarterly ticket base; MICE events with MEA/PSUs; rail-based luxury tourism (Maharajas’ Express, Bharat Gaurav)","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["Q2FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"IRCTC delivered stable 7.7% revenue growth and expanding margins driven by digital ticketing leadership and tourism recovery, with a transformative payment aggregator license pending RBI final approval — a high-impact catalyst that could redefine its revenue model beyond rail-centric services.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":0.0,"fy":"FY23","mcap":45824,"opm":39.4,"pe":45.6,"roe":40.6},{"de":0.0,"fy":"FY24","mcap":74376,"opm":38.3,"pe":66.9,"roe":38.9},{"de":0.0,"fy":"FY25","mcap":58200,"opm":38.1,"pe":44.3,"roe":38.2},{"de":0.02,"fy":"FY26","mcap":44224,"opm":31.9,"pe":31.7,"roe":34.6}],"wtt":null},"drhp":{"rpt":{"financials":{"_source":"ledger","balance_sheet_key":[{"basis":"Standalone","cwip_amount_rs":162100000,"equity_share_capital_amount_rs":1600000000,"fy":"FY2020","inventory_amount_rs":97600000,"net_fixed_assets_amount_rs":1558500000,"networth_amount_rs":13278200000,"other_equity_amount_rs":11678200000,"total_assets_amount_rs":32498400000,"trade_payables_amount_rs":1695400000,"trade_receivables_amount_rs":7894100000},{"basis":"Standalone","cwip_amount_rs":243000000,"equity_share_capital_amount_rs":1600000000,"fy":"FY2021","inventory_amou